  "narrative": "All returned estimates are already signed to the claim direction. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed value means the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast was negative, i.e. the exposed group had a more negative composite dependency score and therefore stronger dependency. For the direction +1 feature_002 claim, a positive signed value means a raw positive contrast, i.e. less negative outcome values and weaker dependency. H155 and H156 are direct context tests of feature_027: in feature_040 >= -7.353 the estimate is +0.878 with interval 0.712 to 1.044 (n 57/943), and in feature_040 <= -7.353 it is +0.730 with interval 0.570 to 0.890 (n 73/927). Both are far above the 0.15 threshold and far from the opposite direction, so I accept and close both; feature_027=1 remains strongly associated with stronger dependency in both median feature_040 strata. H158 and H159 test feature_027 and feature_037 in the extreme feature_053==10 stratum. feature_027 gives +0.744 (0.584 to 0.904; n 72/1108), and feature_037 gives +0.793 (0.709 to 0.877; n 255/925). These are large, precise enough, and consistent with previously validated main effects, so I accept and close both, while noting feature_027 cells remain rare and these are dataset-internal subgroup associations only. H163 accepts feature_002=1 as weaker dependency in feature_040 <= -7.353: +0.756 (0.661 to 0.850; n 199/801), completing the feature_002 feature_040 stratum pair. For feature_063, the main effect is already validated, but these subgroup results require careful threshold and multiplicity judgment. H161 in feature_040 >= -7.353 is +0.306 with interval 0.168 to 0.444 (n 136/864); the lower bound is above the threshold, so I accept this context. H162 in feature_040 <= -7.353 is +0.143 with interval 0.010 to 0.277 (n 130/870); the point is below 0.15 and the interval is compatible with no meaningful effect, so I reject the claimed threshold-sized association in that stratum without treating it as proof of absence. H160 in feature_053==10 is +0.201 with interval 0.088 to 0.315; the point exceeds threshold but the lower bound is substantially below it, and feature_063 has been tested across many strata, so I leave it unresolved and deferred rather than accept it now. H157 is more central because it is the complementary low feature_051 stratum for a marker whose high feature_051 subgroup is already accepted: +0.249 with interval 0.114 to 0.385 (n 127/873). The point is threshold-sized and consistent with the main effect, but the lower bound is below 0.15, so I keep it unresolved and request independent validation to determine whether the feature_063 association is stable across the feature_051 median. The categorical contrast H164 for feature_059 level_001 vs level_003 is +0.0455 with interval -0.028 to 0.119, so it rejects the claimed association. H168 and H169 are essentially null: feature_052 level_001 vs level_003 is -0.0008 (CI -0.123 to 0.122), and feature_054 level_002 vs level_003 is +0.0001 (CI -0.083 to 0.083); both reject the registered claims. Overall, these results strengthen within-data context stability for feature_027, feature_037, feature_002, and partially feature_063, but they do not support causal interpretation, coding-level meaning, biological mechanism, or external generalizability.",
